# The journal, through the real keys (docs/STORY.md §7): what was said to
# somebody and what was read off a thing, kept on the slate where both can be
# read again after walking away from them.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/journal.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --folk=6 --put=sign
#
# The same staging as tours/story.tour: --folk rings villagers round the player,
# one of them a keeper with a conversation written for them, and --put stands a
# notice where it can be walked to. The conversation comes first for the reason
# that tour gives: `use` answers whatever is nearest, so a notice read first
# would be read again by the next press.
#
# Nothing here names a fragment, a beat or an answer: the journal opens on what
# was found last and the rest is reached by walking its list, so a writer can
# change every word the story holds and this still proves the same page.
coast calm
wait 0.6

# --- somebody says something, and the player says something back ----------------------
try 4
  walkto folk 6
  press use
  await talking 3
end
wait 0.4
# The first reply three times over: it goes somewhere each time, and the third
# is the player telling them the tide came in at the same minute twice.
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
shot 01-an-answer-given with talking
press pause
wait 0.5

# --- a thing with words on it ------------------------------------------------------------
near sign
press use
await reading 4
wait 0.4
shot 02-words-on-a-notice with reading
press use
wait 0.5

# --- the journal, on its own key -----------------------------------------------------------
# It opens on what was found last, which is the notice: its words come back on the
# spare pane exactly as they were written, blank lines and all.
tap journal
await app:journal 3
wait 0.3
shot 03-the-notice-kept with app:journal,journal:read

# Down the list: what the player said, and what it was said to.
tap move_down
wait 0.3
shot 04-what-was-said with app:journal,journal:said

# Up past the notice to what the talk taught: a beat, under its arc's title, and
# nothing of the arc that has not happened yet.
tap move_up
wait 0.2
tap move_up
wait 0.3
shot 05-what-is-known-now with app:journal,journal:beat

tap journal
await app:none 3
wait 0.3

# --- and from home, the way a player who has forgotten the key finds it ----------------------
tap pause
await app:pause 3
choose journal
tap use
await app:journal 3
wait 0.3
shot 06-over-home with app:journal
tap pause
await app:pause 3
tap pause
await app:none 3
wait 0.3
shot 07-back-to-the-world with app:none
